+### Swappable optimizer slots
+
+Token reduction has three slots: **input** (the prompt), **context** (what an agent carries between turns) and **output** (tool output). Each slot names the optimizer it uses, so a tool such as RTK or headroom can be started with and swapped later without code changes.
+
+```toml
+# .ta/daemon.toml
+[optimizers.input]
+use = "headroom"   # none | headroom | rtk | proxy
+
+[optimizers.context]
+use = "none"
+
+[optimizers.output]
+use = "none"
+```
+
+- `none` turns the slot off. It is the baseline: input is returned unchanged and nothing is started.
+- `headroom` runs the built-in headroom proxy (or your `[compression.plugin]` block, if you have one).
+- `rtk` and `proxy` run the proxy described by `[compression.plugin]`, which is the `proxy` kind of the input slot. Give it `command`, `args`, `proxy_base_url` and `health_endpoint`.
+- With no `[optimizers]` section the input slot is `headroom`, as before.
+
+`ta compression status` shows the slot selection and the licence of the selected optimizer.
+
+| Optimizer | Slot | Kind | Licence |
+|-----------|------|------|---------|
+| `none` | input, context, output | built in | Apache-2.0 |
+| `headroom` | input | proxy | Apache-2.0 |
+| `rtk` | input | proxy | MIT |
+| `proxy` | input | proxy | that of the tool you configure |
+
+Check the upstream project for its current licence before adopting a tool.
+
+**Reversible reductions.** Optimizers that run inside TA (through the `ta-context-opt` crate) keep the full original on disk under `.ta/compression/originals/<sha256>` and report `{bytes_in, bytes_out, est_tokens_in, est_tokens_out, ms, lossless, original_ref}` for every call. `original_ref` recovers the exact original, so any reduction can be undone and audited. Proxy optimizers compress on the wire and report their own figures through `ta compression status`.
+
+**Testing a slot on identical work.** A golden replay can switch the input slot for one run:
+
+```bash
+ta golden replay <id> --set optimizers.input.use=none --tag no-optimizer
+```
+
+The replayed goal talks to the API directly. An unknown name (for example `rtkk`) is refused before anything runs, and the error lists the valid choices. A replay can turn the proxy off or use the one the daemon already runs; to try a different proxy, set it in `daemon.toml` and run `ta daemon restart`.
+
